Where it truly helps the listener, refer to an earlier episode in the dialogue, e.g. when a concept was explained there, when it gives a useful contrast, or when this episode answers a question it left open ("in our episode on … we …"). Use its title or topic in words, never the ID. Usually zero to three references are right; never force one.
Before you refer to an episode, Read its detailed summary `library/<ID>.md` (it says what was said and which analogies were used), so you get the facts right and can call back an analogy instead of repeating it. Do not read the summaries of episodes you do not refer to. List every episode the dialogue refers to in `episode_references`, with its ID.
